        "node_id": "n_1_ee6b3d",
        "thought_text": "Use a binary search approach to find the minimum number of days. Start with a range from 0 to max(p/a_i, q/b_i) for all i, and iteratively narrow down the range until the difference between the upper and lower bounds is within the acceptable error margin.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794412092.674752
      },
      "rev_n_2_beab61_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_beab61_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_beab61",
        "thought_text": "Formulate the problem as a linear programming problem where we minimize the total number of days while satisfying the constraints of accumulating at least p experience points and q dollars. Use a solver to find the optimal solution.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794412092.674773
